      "content": "That's a good start, the tone is definitely right. However, my supervisor just flagged the draft because the \"Citation Coverage Score\" came back way too low. It's currently around 7/30, which makes the review look really shallow. \n\nCould you expand on this? I need you to integrate more of the names from that list into the discussion so the score goes up, but please—I'm serious—don't just jam them in there. It has to stay academic. For example, you could talk about how Burt's structural holes or Waldinger's work on networks fit into the broader debate. Try to get that score much higher while keeping the actual sociological synthesis strong.",
